                    <div class="u-mt-32">
                        <section data-title="Data availability"><div class="c-article-section" id="data-availability-section"><h2 class="c-article-section__title js-section-title js-c-reading-companion-sections-item" id="data-availability">Data availability</h2><div class="c-article-section__content" id="data-availability-content">
            
            <p>Raw mass spectrometry proteomics data have been deposited in the ProteomeXchange Consortium available via iProX (<a href="http://www.iprox.cn//page/SCV017.html?query=IPX0007409000">IPX0007409000</a>). The PTDS protein matrix and associated resources are available for academic and non-commercial use through the open-access platform <a href="http://db.prottalks.com">db.prottalks.com</a>. Other data used are available from the Kyoto Encyclopedia of Genes and Genomes pathway at <a href="http://www.genome.jp/kegg/pathway.html">https://www.genome.jp/kegg/pathway.html</a> (ref. <sup><a data-track="click" data-track-action="reference anchor" data-track-label="link" data-test="citation-ref" aria-label="Reference 57" title="Kanehisa, M. &amp; Goto, S. KEGG: Kyoto Encyclopedia of Genes and Genomes. Nucleic Acids Res. 28, 27–30 (2000)." href="/articles/s41586-026-11001-9#ref-CR57" id="ref-link-section-d121000133e5941">57</a></sup>), from Metascape at <a href="http://metascape.org/gp/">https://metascape.org/gp/</a> (ref. <sup><a data-track="click" data-track-action="reference anchor" data-track-label="link" data-test="citation-ref" aria-label="Reference 58" title="Zhou, Y. et al. Metascape provides a biologist-oriented resource for the analysis of systems-level datasets. Nat. Commun. 10, 1523 (2019)." href="/articles/s41586-026-11001-9#ref-CR58" id="ref-link-section-d121000133e5953">58</a></sup>), from STRING at <a href="http://cn.string-db.org/">https://cn.string-db.org/</a> (ref. <sup><a data-track="click" data-track-action="reference anchor" data-track-label="link" data-test="citation-ref" aria-label="Reference 59" title="Szklarczyk, D. et al. The STRING database in 2023: protein–protein association networks and functional enrichment analyses for any sequenced genome of interest. Nucleic Acids Res. 51, D638–D646 (2023)." href="/articles/s41586-026-11001-9#ref-CR59" id="ref-link-section-d121000133e5964">59</a></sup>) and from Ingenuity Pathway Analysis at <a href="http://www.ingenuity.com">http://www.ingenuity.com</a> (ref. <sup><a data-track="click" data-track-action="reference anchor" data-track-label="link" data-test="citation-ref" aria-label="Reference 60" title="Kramer, A., Green, J., Pollard, J. Jr. &amp; Tugendreich, S. Causal analysis approaches in ingenuity pathway analysis. Bioinformatics 30, 523–530 (2014)." href="/articles/s41586-026-11001-9#ref-CR60" id="ref-link-section-d121000133e5975">60</a></sup>).</p>
          </div></div></section><section data-title="Code availability"><div class="c-article-section" id="code-availability-section"><h2 class="c-article-section__title js-section-title js-c-reading-companion-sections-item" id="code-availability">Code availability</h2><div class="c-article-section__content" id="code-availability-content">
            
            <p>The project data analysis codes are available via GitHub at <a href="https://github.com/guomics-lab/PTV-1">https://github.com/guomics-lab/PTV-1</a>.</p>
          </div></div></section><div id="MagazineFulltextArticleBodySuffix"><section aria-labelledby="Bib1" data-title="References"><div class="c-article-section" id="Bib1-section"><h2 class="c-article-section__title js-section-title js-c-reading-companion-sections-item" id="Bib1">References</h2><div class="c-article-section__content" id="Bib1-content"><div data-container-section="references"><ol class="c-article-references" data-track-component="outbound reference" data-track-context="references section"><li class="c-article-references__item js-c-reading-companion-references-item" data-counter="1."><p class="c-article-references__text" id="ref-CR1">Bunne, C. et al. How to build the virtual cell with artificial intelligence: priorities and opportunities. <i>Cell</i> <b>187</b>, 7045–7063 (2024).</p><p class="c-article-references__links u-hide-print"><a data-track="click_references" rel="nofollow noopener" data-track-label="10.1016/j.cell.2024.11.015" data-track-item_id="10.1016/j.cell.2024.11.015" data-track-value="article reference" data-track-action="article reference" href="https://doi.org/10.1016%2Fj.cell.2024.11.015" aria-label="Article reference 1" data-doi="10.1016/j.cell.2024.11.015">Article</a> 
